Template: session-service-node/ip-address
Type: string
Description: Enter your service node publicly accessible IPv4 address
 Loki service nodes now require your public IP address to broadcast to the
 network so that remote hosts can connect directly to your service node for
 network services like lokinet routing and the oxen storage server.
 .
 This script can attempt to automatically look up your public IPv4 address
 using an online service (www.ipify.org), or you can enter your address
 manually.  To perform an automatic lookup, leave this field blank.
 .
 To provide an IP address manually enter it now.

Template: session-service-node/confirm-ip-lookup
Type: boolean
Default: true
Description: Use this Service Node public IP?
 The online lookup gave us the following public IPv4 address for this host:
 .
 ${IP}

Template: session-service-node/ip-lookup-failed
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Retry IP address entry/lookup?
 Automatic IP lookup failed:
 .
 ${REASON}
 .
 Do you want to go back and enter an IP manually (or try automatic lookup
 again)?  Note that if you say no here you will have to update the
 /etc/oxen/oxen.conf file yourself with the IP before oxend will start
 properly.

Template: session-service-node/invalid-ip
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Retry IP address entry?
 Invalid IPv4 address entered.
 .
 You entered an invalid IPv4 address.  Choose yes here to return to the IP
 entry dialog and try again (or to use the automatic lookup service).  If
 you say no here your oxend will not start until you manually update the
 /etc/oxen/oxen.conf file yourself with a valid public IP.

Template: session-service-node/l2-provider
Type: string
Description: Enter your Arbitrum One RPC provider URL(s)
 Oxen 11.2+ (as part of a Session service node) requires an Arbitrum One RPC
 provider to retrieve Ethereum L2 registration data.
 .
 Please enter a provider URL (this typically starts http:// or https://).
 .
 If you want to configure backup providers then list them here after the
 primary L2 provider, separated with spaces.
 .
 If you want to update these later, these providers are listed in the
 /etc/oxen/oxen.conf configuration file.
 .
 For advanced setups using oxend L2 proxies enter l2-oxend= followed by
 the proxy address(es).

Template: session-service-node/no-l2-provider
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Provide an Arbitrum L2 URL?
 Oxen 11.2+ (as part of a Session service node) requires an Arbitrum One RPC
 provider to retrieve Ethereum L2 registration data.
 .
 Are you sure you want to leave this blank?  A Session service node will not
 start until a provider is entered via the `l2-provider=` option in
 /etc/oxen/oxen.conf.

Template: session-service-node/bad-l2-provider
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Provide another Arbitrum L2 provider URL?
 The Arbitrum One L2 provider URL(s) you entered do not appear to be working:
 .
 ${ERROR}
 .
 Do you want to go back and edit the L2 provider URL?  Note that if you say
 no here your Session service node will not function properly until the URL
 is updated in /etc/oxen/oxen.conf, or the provider becomes available.
